Several data sets shipped with this project are derived from material published
by HPE Aruba Networking. They are included for interoperability and security
reference, remain the property of their respective owners, and are NOT licensed
under the Apache License that covers this project's own code:

  * aos8_auditor/controls/*.yaml
    The control definitions restate technical hardening recommendations as
    machine-checkable rules, drawn from two source documents: the "ArubaOS
    Hardening Guide" (Aruba Federal Technology Guide, AOS 8.2, doc v1.0,
    2020-01-13) and the "ArubaOS 8 Controller Hardening Guide" (rev 10, January
    2023). Control titles, expected states, and verification commands describe
    factual device configuration. The guides themselves remain the authoritative
    statement of that guidance.

  * aos8_auditor/data/open_ports.yaml
    aos8_auditor/data/scanner_false_positives.yaml
    Transcriptions of the open-port and common-false-positive reference tables
    from the 2023 guide named above, held as offline reference data.

  * aos8_auditor/advisories/aos8_workarounds.csv
    Advisory identifiers, vulnerability titles, and workaround text reproduced
    from published HPE Aruba Networking security advisories (2021-2026). This is
    a point-in-time snapshot and is not updated automatically. Refer to the
    vendor's security advisory portal for the authoritative and current text:
    https://www.arubanetworks.com/support-services/security-bulletins/

CVE identifiers are assigned by the CVE Program (https://www.cve.org/).
